    "perplexity": {
      "description": "An Ending is the sixth and final studio album by Lonely Robot, the progressive-rock project led by John Mitchell. Released through Wild Thyme Records, it brings the project’s long-running astronaut narrative to its conclusion, following a solitary figure traveling through space while reflecting on humanity, identity, and the possibility of home. The album’s atmosphere is cinematic and contemplative, combining melodic rock songwriting with expansive keyboards, polished guitar work, and a strong sense of science-fiction scale.\n\nRather than ending in grandiose triumph, An Ending emphasizes acceptance, grief, and peace. Songs such as “This World Window,” “Show the Way,” “Ad Astra,” and “The River” balance accessible rock melodies with introspective, emotionally weighty arrangements. As the closing statement of Lonely Robot’s conceptual arc, the album has been received as a poignant and fitting farewell—an album that transforms a space odyssey into a meditation on isolation, human frailty, and reconciliation.",
